homelab-calendar (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Search (post-cutover #87): the dialog is a form with a Search button and
    the keyboard's Go key runs it (the only button was Done, which closed it:
    found by Gardner on Android); every typed word must match, in the title,
    the place, the notes or the people invited, over calendars, shared
    calendars and single events shared with you; with AI on, "related by
    meaning" follows (relate: "doctor" finds the infusion at the hospital),
    on the page, in the API (related=1) and in the CLI.
  * Local time zone (#88): every account's zone is Local, the device's own as
    the browser reports it (migration 008 clears the zones the page itself had
    saved on first visits); a fixed zone stays available in Settings and from
    the zone code ("CST") after the view switcher, which opens the zone dialog;
    the page follows the device when the tab is next looked at and reports
    the device's zone so reminders are written in it; the zone from My Account
    is only the mail fallback now, not an override.
  * Pinned events and the zone of a place (#89): an event can be pinned to
    its own zone and then reads that zone's clock wherever you are ("1:30 PM
    CST" with a pin mark, in every view; the peek says both clocks); an update
    without a zone keeps the event's own (a drag in a grid shown in Montana no
    longer re-zones a Kansas appointment: times_zone); the editor shows an
    existing event's clocks in its own zone; mail proposals carry the zone the
    AI read off the email's address, and the editor's "From the address" asks
    the AI for it (zone-for-place).

