homelab-calendar (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Invitations (post-cutover #85): invite people to an event (the editor's
    Invite field, with free/busy for accounts here; the CLI); each gets an
    email with Yes / Maybe / No links and an iCalendar REQUEST part (their
    mail program's own buttons work too); /i/<token> is the invitation page;
    a change re-invites (SEQUENCE+1 and a fresh answer when the time or place
    changed), a delete sends a CANCEL, the organizer is told of every answer
    (mail, and the webhook when set); answers mailed back (METHOD:REPLY) are
    applied from the milter's inbox table. Migration 007: events.sequence,
    event_attendees, notice_queue, itip_inbox. Needs homelab-common >= 0.1.37.
  * Fix: with the database session in America/Chicago (production's setting)
    every change to an event counted as a time change, because the row's
    starts_at text (-06) was compared with the new value (+00) as strings:
    a retitle of a repeating event dropped its moved and cancelled
    occurrences, and emptied its reminder queue. Instants are now compared
    as instants. Found by t/model.t against a scratch PostgreSQL in that zone.

